# Voice dictation and project terminology

The maintainer may use **voice dictation** (e.g. Wispr Flow). Spoken names are sometimes transcribed with **phonetic** or approximate spellings.

**When a word in the user message sounds like a known project or tool name in context, assume the canonical spelling** and proceed without pedantic correction in replies unless clarification is needed.

Examples (non-exhaustive):

| Often heard / transcribed | Intended |
|---------------------------|----------|
| Kadi, Caddie, Katy | **Caddy** (reverse proxy / TLS) |
| iziki, easy key, Ez Key | **Ezkey** (project name) |
| Light sail | **Lightsail** (AWS) |
| Wisp, whisper | **Wispr** (if referring to Wispr Flow) |

Prefer interpreting **technical discussion** (deploy, TLS, compose, API hostnames) through this lens rather than treating odd spellings as unrelated proper nouns.
